Description: Computes travel-time matrices, accessibility and trip-by-trip
    (expanded and arrival) matrices on multimodal transport networks (walk,
    bike, car and public transport) built from 'OpenStreetMap' extracts and
    'GTFS' feeds. The routing engine is written in 'Rust', runs in the R
    session without a 'Java' runtime, keeps the network in memory, and is
    shared with the 'Python' package of the same name. The engine is a port of
    'R5', and the functions, their arguments and their results follow the
    'r5r' package.
